From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:27:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Describe the system sleep
 controls

Describe, for the J604 only, what apple_cpu, apple-sleep and apple-s2r
need, from the J604's own data:

 - the PMGR CPU start/stop block at PMGR + 0x34000 (the offset m1n1
   starts the J604's CPUs with; inside the ADT PMGR range 0x380730000),
   and the per-core implementation registers from the ADT ranges
   0x210050000.. (E0-E5) and 0x211050000.. (P0-P3). No ACC ranges, so
   no cluster gating on CPU offline;
 - the PMGR sleep counters (ADT range 0x3882c8000 = PMGR_AON + 0x48000),
   AP wake source block (ADT range 0x388004000) and sleep exit times (ADT
   range 0x380760000 = PMGR + 0x60000), with the ADT's own
   "ap-wake-sources" list unchanged. No CPM range: the T6020 CPM gating
   words are not known on T8132 and are not guessed;
 - the suspend-to-RAM node without clock generator, PLL and timer
   registers (not found in the J604 ADT at the T6021 offsets) and
   without apple,cluster-power-state (so the CPU cluster power-down is left out
   until the J604 probe locates the words), CPU clusters 0/1 in the ADT
   "soc-clusters" order, the SEP power state and the watchdog. It is a root node because it has no registers; the
   binding's node name pattern allows that.

Register offsets inside each block follow T6020 and are TO-VERIFY on the
J604 before suspend-to-RAM is used (bring-up kit, read-only first step).

The timer keeps ticking: H16 has a continuous hardware clock (XNU
HAS_CONTINUOUS_HWCLOCK), so arm,no-tick-in-suspend is not set.

Default boots are unchanged: apple-sleep stages are off, apple-s2r needs
apple_s2r.enable=1, and CPUs only go offline on request.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 .../bindings/arm/apple/apple,cpu-ctrl.yaml    |   4 +-
 .../bindings/power/apple,pmgr-s2r.yaml        |   2 +-
 .../boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-sleep.dtsi      | 104 ++++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts      |   2 +
 4 files changed, 110 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-sleep.dtsi

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/apple/apple,cpu-ctrl.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/apple/apple,cpu-ctrl.yaml
index 762d8d49f6..3a9ed57511 100644
